  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 42a7ef911f4c60e408989a759d2b9b18, type: 3}
  m_Name: SQL_UPDATE
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CodeEscape.Programming.LessonData
  id: SQL_UPDATE
  language: 3
  conceptTitle: 'UPDATE: Changing Data'
  symbol: UPDATE
  relatedQuestionIds:
  - SQL_06_UPDATE
  topics:
  - UPDATE
  definition: UPDATE changes values in rows that are already in a table.
  howItWorks: 'Write UPDATE and the table''s name, then SET column = new value. Add
    WHERE with a condition to choose which rows change. Be careful: without WHERE,
    UPDATE changes every row in the table.'
  exampleCode: "Table: pets\n id | name  | animal | age\n  1 | Bolt  | Dog    |  
    4\n  2 | Misty | Cat    |   2\n\nUPDATE pets\nSET age = 3\nWHERE name = 'Misty';"
  exampleExplanation: Only Misty's row matches WHERE name = 'Misty', so only her
    age changes, from 2 to 3. Bolt's row is not touched.
  tip: 'Before you run an UPDATE, read the WHERE line: it decides which rows change.'
